    "model": {
      "id": "arithmetic-circuit-complex",
      "version": "1",
      "description": "Multiply two n by n complex matrices exactly with division-free arithmetic circuits. Scalar addition, subtraction and multiplication each cost one; inputs and constants are free. For every epsilon > 0, one positive constant C bounds the cost by C n^(t+epsilon) for every positive size n. Results over every field qualify by specialization to the complex numbers.",
